      "message": "**String termination in `FtGetBootVersion` (`updater.cc`)** You are guaranteeing a null-terminator at the very end of the buffer using `data.back() \u003d \u0027\\0\u0027`. However, if the device returns a short version string followed by uninitialized garbage (instead of null-padding), `std::string` will include that garbage until it hits the final byte.\n\n* **Fix:** Read up to the first null byte explicitly.\n\n```c\nauto null_pos \u003d std::ranges::find(data, \u0027\\0\u0027);\nstd::string version(data.begin(), null_pos);\n\n```",
